invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_inverse.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_inverse_steps
reason: the approximations' shifts stop a bit short, so the top bit of a | b
  ends at bit 126 of the pair and an approximation keeps 32 of the value's
  top bits where the bound spec/lean/Spec/P256WideInverse.lean proves reads
  33. p256_wide_inverse_steps holds the approximations to a reference that
  reads the 33 bits from the bit length of a | b, over every a and b. Each
  run is a proof, so this belongs to the nightly's
  test-invariants-proof-backed job.

--- old
        uint64_t mask = ~nonzero_mask((a_high | b_high) >> (64 - s));
--- new
        uint64_t mask = ~nonzero_mask((a_high | b_high) >> (63 - s));
